## DRAFTER'S READINGS (for Tuesday's stamp read; each is the drafter's, MEASURED or READ ONLY as marked; Tuesday strikes any it disagrees with, and the line "STAMP READING" in the Stamp then says which)
1. **B538-8: the ruling's proviso fires, so the brief builds nothing for it (READ, MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER 18:2x).** The B518 brief, `-216` item, says "refuse a string that is not exactly one member name (no comma list, no trimming)", and its property rows say "(b) for every enum-typed member read through the API, every string that is not exactly one member name gives 400 (-216)" (brief line 59). The builder's committed property row `QuoteInputHardening.Enums.cs:195` (`Only_the_exact_name_the_contract_lists_reads_and_every_other_string_or_number_is_refused`) asserts that an upper-case and a lower-case spelling of every contract enum's every name (the census asserts `TierOverride` is among them, `:202`; the refused set is built at `:216-219`) is refused. Restoring base for `Auto`/`Core`/`Growth`/`Scale` would turn that committed row red, and the standing rule is "never loosen an assertion". The gate's own fix-shape for B538-8 is "none needed; state it in the API notes". So the seat quotes the scope in DESIGN, keeps the head, records it as a Note for the records seat, and builds no change. **If Tuesday strikes this reading at the stamp, the alternative is in item (8) below.**
2. **B538-10: the proviso does not fire, so base is restored.** The scope names a null SKU only (B518 brief, `-217`: "a care row with a null `sku` is served without it though the contract requires it", acceptance "a null `sku` is refused"). The base had no SKU check of any kind (`e027ebd0:ReferenceStoreDocument.cs:99`, MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER), and a blank-SKU row taking every catalogue route down is a worse failure than the row it guards.
3. **B538-1 leaves two cases with no approved wording, and the brief folds them into ONE sentence (item 1 of the order).** With the name never printed, a nested unknown member reads through the approved template `... contract: {path} is not valid.` (WORDS-DRAFT row 8, "a mapping failure not listed above") with `{path}` = the parent path, e.g. `bomLines[0] is not valid.` That is the approved text byte for byte. At the ROOT (`{"x":1}` on create) there is no parent path, and the code's existing fallback is the approved `The request body is not valid JSON.`, which is untrue for a body that is valid JSON. The B538-3 root case (a body that is a string, number, array or boolean) has the same gap. So ONE replacement sentence, if no approved sentence fits, must cover both root cases. This is the drafter's extension of ruling 3; it keeps the new words at one sentence as ruled.
4. **A consequence the product owner should know (FOR TUESDAY, not for the seat to decide):** after ruling 1 the approved row-6 sentence (`... contract: bomLines[0].price is not a field the contract has.`) is unreachable, and a typo in a field name is reported as `bomLines[0] is not valid.`, which tells the caller less. The alternative that keeps row 6 and stays bounded is the gate's second shape (print the name only when it is at most 40 characters of `[A-Za-z0-9_]`; any other name falls back to the parent path). The brief follows the ruling as written.
5. **B538-2: one TOTAL cap of 20 null-entry errors across all lists, and no new word.** A per-list cap would still allow 12 lists x 20 errors; a total cap is the simplest bound. The sentence of each listed error is unchanged (`{list}[{i}] must not be null.`); no "and N more" line is added (that would be a new word).
6. **B538-4: `IsDocumentFault` is NOT yours.** It is defined at `SourceDocumentChecks.cs:190` (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER), a lane B520/PR #100 file whose fix round is live (B541) and whose brief fences `EngineRead`'s and `IsDocumentFault`'s signature AND meaning (`ActiveSources.Load` calls them). The ruling says "ActiveSources.cs (IsDocumentFault misses ...)": read it as "the start catch in `ActiveSources.cs`". The unreadable-file case is handled by a second catch in `ActiveSources.Load` (your file); the null-block case by a guard in `ReferenceStoreDocument.cs` / `ActiveSourceSet.From`. **No file outside PR #102's 14 paths is needed for any of the seven items** (the new test files below are in the builder brief's four new-file families, so they add paths but no new family).
7. **B538-13 may need a one-line test seam, which is a `src` change the ruling allows only if a row proves it is needed.** The duplicate site's row reaches its fault by storing a legacy quote with an undefined enum (`QuoteInputHardening.Enums.cs:133-144`); the create site has no such door (the binder refuses that value, which is why the gate graded it unreachable). The seat tries a seam-free row first and proves it cannot be built (what it tried, the output); only then a seam with the precedent `SourceDocumentChecks.AfterEngineRead` (null in production, one line, no behaviour, no words, listed in DESIGN).
8. **ALTERNATIVE for item 1, only if Tuesday's stamp reading says RESTORE for B538-8:** make the name set of `ExactEnumName<T>` (`ApiJson.cs:54-56`) compare `OrdinalIgnoreCase` for a member WITHOUT a `JsonStringEnumMemberName` attribute (base's stock behaviour) and keep exact, case-sensitive matching for renamed members (base refused `"Software"` for the renamed member too); then the committed property row at `Enums.cs:195` goes red for plain members and must be changed to expect base's behaviour (print every changed line and why), `Auto`/`AUTO`/`auto` get their own rows, and the gate's mutant "names case-insensitive" changes meaning. Do not build this unless the Stamp says so.

